The worked seam `tm-oracle plan` applies AFTER `plan-seam.patch` and `p64-runs.patch`
(stage 6 W-44 track C, README gap 4507).  `build-oracle.sh` applies it with `git apply`
and FAILS the build when it does not apply, and the stamp carries its hash.

The comparand moves the running estimate by what FORK 4748911 reads as the running
block's worked minutes (parity P55 and P46 read that reading; README gap 4247), so the
oracle answers it as the `worked` op.  Fork `active_run` reads it in its own body -- a
private method of the private `Planner`, the reading held in a local -- so until W-44 the
oracle's `worked_one` RE-TYPED its selection (the log's open block when it is the
state's running item, else the clock since `started` on the planned date): a frozen
comparand partly computed by code this repository owns, which is the shape the campaign
names "a comparison that compares the kernel with itself" (README gap 4507).

This graft makes the fork's OWN lines reachable, and changes none of them: the two
statements `active_run` read the reading with are MOVED, character for character, into
a method of `Planner` that `active_run` now calls, so the planner and the oracle run one
body; and one public entry builds the fork's own `Planner` for a `PlanInput` and asks it.
Nothing else in the fork is touched.  `planner_classes.rs`' check of this file holds
the move to that property: every line the graft removes is a line it adds, in order.

